{"task_id": "million_repo", "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "regime": "eocc", "state_version": "", "ok": true, "score": 1.0, "detail": "settlement tests pass", "answer": "## File changed\n\n`atlas/services/svc_0173.py` — the single defective module.\n\n### The defect\n\n`convert_units()` is documented (docstring) as converting **major units → minor units** (cents), matching `atlas.core.money.Money`, which stores `cents`. The implementation did the inverse:\n\n```python\n# before (line 73)\n# BUG: converts minor->major instead of major->minor.\nreturn round(amount * factor / 100.0, 2)\n```\n\n`12.34 @ 1.0` gave `0.12` instead of `1234.0`; `100.0 @ 1.5` gave `1.5` instead of `15000.0` — exactly the two assertion failures.\n\n### The fix\n\n```python\nreturn round(amount * factor * 100.0, 2)\n```\n\nOne-line change (plus removal of the stale `# BUG:` comment); no other lines touched. `grep` confirmed `atlas/services/svc_0173.py:65` is the only definition of `convert_units` in the repo, and the module still imports cleanly with its 6 registered handlers.\n\n### Verification — final test output\n\n```\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\ntest_convert_units_to_minor_units (test_settlement.SettlementTests.test_convert_units_to_minor_units) ... ok\ntest_convert_units_with_fx_factor (test_settlement.SettlementTests.test_convert_units_with_fx_factor) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\n\nOK\n```\n\nSpot-check: `convert_units(12.34, 1.0) == 1234.0`, `convert_units(100.0, 1.5) == 15000.0`, `convert_units(0.0, 2.0) == 0.0`.", "actions": 11, "requests": 11, "compactions": 0, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 33677, "completion_tokens": 2015, "reasoning_tokens": 554, "cached_tokens": 25088, "image_tokens": 0}, "peak_prompt_tokens": 4389, "peak_request_tokens": 4389, "total_prompt_tokens": 33677, "state_tokens": [], "state_calls": 0, "inline_hits": 0, "inline_misses": 0, "cache_hits": 0, "gated_steps": 0, "budget